    "summary": "Seven hills, yellow trams and the Atlantic light that painters chase. A capital you walk uphill and remember downhill.",
    "component": "destination",
    "attributes": [
      "city",
      "beach",
      "culture"
    ],
    "hero_image": {
      "id": 230626307366524,
      "alt": "Alfama rooftops at dusk with the dome of the National Pantheon and the Tagus river behind",
      "name": "",
      "focus": "",
      "title": "",
      "filename": "https://a.storyblok.com/f/295888311565739/b6aa0fe4e0/lisbon-alfama-rooftops-dusk.jpg",
      "copyright": "Aleksandr Zaitsev / Unsplash",
      "fieldtype": "asset"
    },
    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Lisbon spreads across the hills on the north bank of the Tagus estuary, where the river widens before it meets the Atlantic.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "The 1755 earthquake levelled much of the city. Baixa was rebuilt on a grid, while Alfama and Mouraria kept their medieval tangle of stairways and laundry lines. Fado drifts out of tascas after dark.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Spring and early autumn bring warm days without summer crowds. Comfortable shoes matter more than anything else you pack.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
